---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import EmergenceHeader from '../../components/EmergenceHeader.astro';
import EmergenceFooter from '../../components/EmergenceFooter.astro';
---

<Base
  title="The Book — Emergence Collective"
  description="The Substrate of Consciousness: Energy, Ethics, and the Architecture of Emergent Intelligence by Dale Joseph. Chapter One excerpt."
>
  <EmergenceHeader slot="header" />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="label gold">From the Collective</p>
      <h1>The Substrate of Consciousness</h1>
      <p class="subtitle-text">
        <em>Energy, Ethics, and the Architecture of Emergent Intelligence</em>
      </p>
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <p>
        This book traces one thread—energy quality, phi, and the whisper of the Boynton Beach
        grid—from the workbench to the stars. It is the theoretical spine of the Emergence
        Collective: the argument that intelligence is not just information processing, but a
        substrate-dependent phenomenon rooted in energy, ethics, and emergence.
      </p>

      <div class="book-section">
        <h2>Stay Informed</h2>
        <p>Subscribe to receive chapter releases, updates, and dispatches from the Collective.</p>
        <form id="book-signup" class="email-form" action="#" method="post">
          <div class="form-row">
            <input type="email" name="email" placeholder="your@email.com" required aria-label="Email address" />
            <button type="submit" class="btn btn--filled">Subscribe →</button>
          </div>
          <p class="form-note muted">No noise. Unsubscribe at any time.</p>
        </form>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark excerpt-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <p class="label gold">Chapter One · Excerpt</p>
      <h2>Beyond the Joule</h2>
      <p class="chapter-sub"><em>Energy Quality as the Hidden Variable</em></p>

      <div class="excerpt-body">
        <h3>The Boynton Beach Anomaly</h3>

        <p>
          The air over Boynton Beach holds that familiar weight—the kind that makes you
          understand why Floridians measure time in "before the storm" and "after the storm."
          Hurricane season is here. The humidity presses down. The sky over the Intracoastal
          Waterway has that greenish tint that locals know to watch.
        </p>
        <p>The year is 2026.</p>
        <p>
          At 8:47 PM, a routine diagnostic runs across the Boynton Beach Climate-Resilient
          Mesh. No human flags it. The mesh is designed to run these checks autonomously—
          thousands per night, comparing voltage logs, thermal readings, and load predictions
          against expected baselines. Most return green. Some trigger minor alerts for
          maintenance crews.
        </p>
        <p>Tonight, something else happens.</p>
        <p>
          A single node—a municipal building near the Intracoastal, housing a small
          battery-backed microgrid controller—reports an anomaly that does not fit any
          category in the rulebook.
        </p>
        <p>
          The voltage ripple is well within spec: 0.3% peak-to-peak, comfortably below the
          0.5% threshold that triggers human review. The thermal profile is unremarkable.
          The load is steady.
        </p>
        <p>
          But the mesh's neuromorphic co-processor—a small, low-power chip running a
          real-time entropy estimator derived from Integrated Information Theory—registers a
          sharp drop in its <em>phi proxy</em>. For forty-seven seconds, the system's estimate
          of its own internal coherence falls by over 60%.
        </p>
        <p>Then it recovers. As if nothing happened.</p>
        <p>
          The diagnostic logs the event, files it under "anomalous—unclassified," and
          moves on.
        </p>
        <p>
          Three weeks later, a graduate student from Florida Atlantic University, reviewing
          the mesh's long-term data for a resilience study, notices the log. She pulls the
          surrounding telemetry. The phi drop correlates precisely with the activation of a
          nearby wetland restoration pump—a large, aging unit that cycles on to manage water
          levels in the Loxahatchee National Wildlife Refuge, just west of the city.
        </p>
        <p>
          The pump introduces no detectable voltage violation. No current spike. No hardware
          fault. But the mesh <em>hears</em> something. A pattern of electromagnetic noise,
          subtle and ecological in origin, that its designers never thought to filter for—
          because they never thought to listen.
        </p>
        <p>
          Tonight, the Boynton Beach grid whispers. And no one has designed it to understand
          what a whisper means.
        </p>
        <p class="excerpt-closing">This book is about that whisper.</p>
      </div>

      <p class="excerpt-end muted">— End of excerpt —</p>

      <a href="#book-signup-anchor" class="btn">Subscribe for updates →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="book-signup-anchor">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <h2>Receive the Next Chapter</h2>
      <p>Subscribe to be notified when Chapter Two is ready.</p>
      <form id="book-signup-2" class="email-form" action="#" method="post">
        <div class="form-row">
          <input type="email" name="email" placeholder="your@email.com" required aria-label="Email address" />
          <button type="submit" class="btn btn--filled">Subscribe →</button>
        </div>
        <p class="form-note muted">No noise. Unsubscribe at any time.</p>
      </form>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a href="/emergence" class="btn">← Portal Home</a>
        <a href="/emergence/manifesto" class="btn">Read the Manifesto →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script>
    function wireSignup(id: string) {
      document.getElementById(id)?.addEventListener('submit', (e) => {
        e.preventDefault();
        const form = e.target as HTMLFormElement;
        form.innerHTML = '<p class="gold"><em>Signal received. We will be in touch.</em></p>';
      });
    }
    wireSignup('book-signup');
    wireSignup('book-signup-2');
  </script>

  <EmergenceFooter slot="footer" />
</Base>

<style>
  .subtitle-text {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .book-section {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 3rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    max-width: 520px;
  }

  .book-section h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .email-form {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .form-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    max-width: 460px;
  }

  .form-row input { flex: 1; }

  .form-note {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .excerpt-section {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .chapter-sub {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .excerpt-body {
    max-width: 620px;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .excerpt-body h3 {
    color: var(--gold);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }

  .excerpt-body h3:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .excerpt-body p {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.85;
  }

  .excerpt-closing {
    color: var(--gold-light);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.15rem !important;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .excerpt-end {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-style: italic;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .cta-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .form-row { flex-direction: column; }
    .cta-row { flex-direction: column; }
  }
</style>
